    "description": {
      "value": "Divine flames scour creatures within the area. Creatures take 6d6 fire damage and 2d6 persistent fire damage. The divine power within the flames scorches the spirit as well; a creature takes spirit damage instead of fire damage from divine immolation if that would be more detrimental to the creature (as determined by the GM).\n\n- **Critical Success:** The creature is unaffected.\n- **Success:** The creature takes half damage and no persistent damage.\n- **Failure:** The creature takes full damage and persistent damage.\n- **Critical Failure:** The creature takes double damage and double persistent damage."
    },
    "higher_level_description": {
      "value": "Heightened (+1): The damage increases by 1d6 and persistent damage increases by 1d6."
    },
